# 4. Tighten Section 6.C (B-17)
old_sec6c = r"""\subsection{Dual-Tier Feasibility Pilots}
Prior to establishing the frozen public benchmark, preliminary pilots evaluated our prototype Regime-Aware Multimodal Proxy architecture (RAMP-RAG) across controlled proxy text (Tier 1: $N=334$ queries) and physical media streams (Tier 2: $N=151$ evaluation probes comprising $N=85$ photo scene-text probes, $N=13$ audio queries from ESC-50 \cite{piczak2015esc50} over 52 raw 44.1\,kHz WAV recordings via LAION-CLAP \cite{wu2023clap}, and $N=53$ visual queries over 191 album photos using CLIP ViT-B/32 \cite{radford2021clip}). Tier-1 proxy lookups produced near-ceiling retrieval across systems (BM25 MRR = 0.9958; pipeline MRR = 0.9970) because queries mirrored catalog annotation strings. On raw physical media (Tier 2), sparse BM25 achieved MRR = 0.7916 on scene text, CLAP achieved MRR = 1.0000 on audio recordings, and CLIP ViT-B/32 achieved Hit@10 = 0.792 (MRR = 0.6182) on raw photographic pixels. Exploratory synthetic noise sweeps ($N=600$) further confirmed sparse resilience (BM25 MRR = 0.9337 under 20\% character noise) over dense baselines (MRR = 0.5306)."""

